nWindows 10 with Nvidia 5090 GPU it’s completely normal\n\nMac with M2 it will become more black as you approach the Default Material or Visual Shader. This has happened on two different setups and is reproducible with any material that has Roughness enabled.\n\n<img width=\"853\" height=\"952\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/2fc2b199-ab7e-48b2-b916-9cf13bdccfb4\" />\n<img width=\"894\" height=\"617\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/908495cb-f84b-4408-9103-b5dfbf9ada7c\" />\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\nCreate a StandardMaterial3D and Turn on Roughness\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nNone","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121662/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121662/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null}